 ```
 
+##### limit
+
+The maximum number of ranges to return, defaults to no limit. Only valid,
+satisfiable ranges are counted (after combining, when `combine` is `true`).
+When a header has more ranges than `limit`, a single range spanning from the
+lowest start to the highest end is returned instead (so the response can be a
+single range rather than multipart). A `limit` that is not a positive integer
+is ignored.
+
+<!-- eslint-disable no-undef -->
+
+```js
+parseRange(1000, 'bytes=500-600,0-10,900-950', { limit: 2 })
+// => [{ start: 0, end: 950 }]
+```
+
